# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no database, no storage bucket and no API key.
#
# The whole inventory is the JSON files in inventory/ and the photos in
# public/inventory/. Everything below is optional except NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,
# which only matters once the site has a real domain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The site's own canonical origin: protocol, no trailing slash. Used for
# canonical tags, Open Graph URLs, JSON-LD and the sitemap.
#
# OPTIONAL ON VERCEL. If unset, the site uses VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL,
# which Vercel supplies automatically and which is the stable production
# domain (not the per-deployment URL, which changes on every push). Set this
# explicitly once there is a real custom domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Placeholder guard (see src/lib/dealer.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# src/lib/dealer.ts ships fictional contact details -- a 555 phone number, a
# reserved .example domain, an invented address -- until the real ones are
# filled in. Publishing those on a live site would point real buyers at a fake
# phone number, so a production deploy refuses to build while they remain.
#
# The guard fires when VERCEL_ENV=production. On a non-Vercel host, set this
# to "true" in the production environment to get the same protection.
REQUIRE_REAL_DEALER_DATA=""

# Escape hatch: set to "true" to deploy with the placeholder details anyway.
# Needed right now, until the dealer's real name, address and phone are in
# src/lib/dealer.ts. Remove it once they are.
ALLOW_PLACEHOLDER_DEALER=""
